#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096502 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96967f25-565a-5338-878e-00fd30055772" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Below a Curve and Above the X-Axis"}] :question/id #uuid "dc29cf6e-4f68-552e-ae7a-f9834eec1bd7" :question/math-academy-id "e-781" :question/problem "Find the area between the curve $y=x^2-2x+2,$ the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=0$ and $x=2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/assets/6b85f10cde49017eac1c56ad1b8abbcdf3033a367d5e1eb162dd89fbb6141461.png)" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}-2x+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-2{\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x+2{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{2}-2\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{2}+2x{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{8}{3}-0)-2(2-0)+2(2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}-4+4 \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096503 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ad216da-1bcf-5b87-9436-918ef1e5015a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Above a Curve and Below the X-Axis"}] :question/id #uuid "5893a692-573a-5e1a-81aa-db34fa6059ed" :question/math-academy-id "e-782" :question/problem "Find the area of the closed region between the curve $y=x^2-1$ and the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the intersections of the curve with the $x$-axis:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-1 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ x & =\\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe draw a sketch of the region, as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/assets/9b78aad41f84f6a6997914bd8d4243f30cb0ebea4edb5305962dc11c7a46a807.png)\n\nWe want the area between the curve $y=x^2-1$ and the $x$-axis, from $x=-1$ to $x=1.$ To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{-1}^{1}-x{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}-(-\\frac{1}{3}))-(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}-2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $\\dfrac{4}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096867 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96967f25-565a-5338-878e-00fd30055772" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Below a Curve and Above the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df635a58-77bf-5e95-a399-dd1baea9994d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093610} {:answer/id #uuid "f08997c9-ba52-53b9-9c33-46805da068a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093611} {:answer/id #uuid "ff97270f-a011-5d06-99d9-c118d5dc4185" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093612} {:answer/id #uuid "1994dce0-f633-5f83-8dbe-b6ffdebda18e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093613} {:answer/id #uuid "752de6cd-f161-5e20-ae88-73328e04a0c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093614}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df635a58-77bf-5e95-a399-dd1baea9994d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093610} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff9da75d-bbb7-5a3d-9a49-484c7a329b2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093609}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fee589a4-db91-599f-87c6-08f88cf08d01" :question/math-academy-id "q-11005" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/assets/e1b6599646532be14e417731c4a8b2f7c4dffcc475e2b99cda0279e7dbf08bc6.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=-3{x}^{2}+5x$, the $x$-axis and the line $x=1$, shown above." :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-3{x}^{2}+5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+5\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{1}+5\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-3(\\frac{1}{3}-0)+5(\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309561 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96967f25-565a-5338-878e-00fd30055772" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Below a Curve and Above the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b8fbd89-d54e-5648-870d-ba6f2405d280" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309563} {:answer/id #uuid "7b61c225-65a5-5356-8d43-8ae8b29aeb9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309564} {:answer/id #uuid "7bb558f3-ba17-5381-8422-37b07e8b8bba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309565} {:answer/id #uuid "95f6b6b0-d6b3-57f3-915d-9af98f3d4aa3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309566} {:answer/id #uuid "432cd216-c1ac-5830-8d28-49a69e72f2aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309567}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b8fbd89-d54e-5648-870d-ba6f2405d280" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309563} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b6077d6-562d-541b-9b6b-447c5f9614e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309562}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "019a0e1c-ba08-5830-ba8d-7a1ca3055587" :question/math-academy-id "q-11006" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/assets/23776e39d83f9feb926b2001b9c763298c8004cad21357433926fb8f40b1ebe7.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{3}$, the $x$-axis and the line $x=2$, shown above." :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}(\\frac{(2)^{4}}{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}(4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309568 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ad216da-1bcf-5b87-9436-918ef1e5015a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Above a Curve and Below the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7b46985-9a46-5801-bcf5-15fb87e5681d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{70}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309570} {:answer/id #uuid "37419c56-6fb0-588f-bf63-d1e487b163f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{29}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309571} {:answer/id #uuid "a47dfcf8-e777-54a5-aebd-1db7745eead3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{29}{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309572} {:answer/id #uuid "91d71b58-f11b-57fa-8df5-1fdeeb3f14e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309573} {:answer/id #uuid "d5b027f7-6f6e-5102-9f7b-550dc3c1a467" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{38}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309574}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7b46985-9a46-5801-bcf5-15fb87e5681d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{70}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309570} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a194efa-80ce-531b-82f0-16cf467051a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309569}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d89a894e-ff6b-5438-9ff0-2e7c6bb9b7d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-11025" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/assets/0775eb4f214e6d4c0388817e59f775d306e647779fe7fb98c856a5a1ab79cb09.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=-2{x}^{2}-9$, the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=2.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(-2{x}^{2}-9)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-9{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{2}-9\\cdot x{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =-2(\\frac{(2)^{3}}{3}-0)-9(2-0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{16}{3}-18 \\\\  & =-\\frac{70}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $\\frac{70}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286993 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96967f25-565a-5338-878e-00fd30055772" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Below a Curve and Above the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ad04aee-4354-5499-a9c4-5d32782153cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{3}+\\ln(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286995}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ad04aee-4354-5499-a9c4-5d32782153cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{3}+\\ln(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286995} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfbc56d0-6cf5-56e8-832a-e1f5ce426489" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286994}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3dc8a6c1-7592-5eeb-a313-53d3c7edaf54" :question/math-academy-id "q-316022" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/assets/b5432ed129d85a3718f8e5ebe0cca141731c366d1b32e8e72d0916c60c34de2c.png)\n\nA region in the $x$-$y$ plane is bounded by the curve $y={sec}^{2}⁡x+\\frac{1}{x}$, and the $x$-axis between $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$, as shown above. \nFind the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}({sec}^{2}⁡(x)+\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)){|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{3})-(\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi /3}{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309575 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ad216da-1bcf-5b87-9436-918ef1e5015a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Above a Curve and Below the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6674705c-28a3-562c-8bd1-67e3f13e2907" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{56}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309577} {:answer/id #uuid "9f091ad2-6197-5914-b32b-7ed6a917757b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6674705c-28a3-562c-8bd1-67e3f13e2907" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{56}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309577} :answer-field/id #uuid "4077d12f-bff4-5de2-8aa1-b365b80dc5aa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309576}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b9764ba6-cf4b-5320-9e3f-a842856afa37" :question/math-academy-id "q-316226" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/assets/0a7a32f856d63403d7125f1c6bb9acc9a5fcd182c2f7fbd3f3ebdfa42f9c9c2c.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ between the curve $y=-{x}^{2}-8$, the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=2$ (shown above). Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$ \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(-{x}^{2}-8)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-8{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{2}-8\\cdot x{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =-(\\frac{(2)^{3}}{3}-0)-8(2-0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{3}-16 \\\\  & =-\\frac{56}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is \n\n$$\nA=-{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{56}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309579 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ad216da-1bcf-5b87-9436-918ef1e5015a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Above a Curve and Below the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4af8112b-bd64-5411-a7e7-7a66654158ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309581} {:answer/id #uuid "c946f0a9-5deb-55c3-8603-752ca595fc45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309582}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4af8112b-bd64-5411-a7e7-7a66654158ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309581} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f95d24b-f17d-5e37-a862-0fa05284d956" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309580}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "74326dd3-adad-5326-940c-9aa17cfe09b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-345385" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/assets/d43d7419f631b479478641ac203c6816693c68ffc40ccc1d4a8a72da0a03461a.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}}}$, the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{3}{2}$, as shown above. Find the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3/2}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{3/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =arccos\\,(\\frac{x}{3}){|}_{0}^{3/2} \\\\  & =arccos\\,(\\frac{1}{2})-arccos\\,(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is \n\n$$\nA=-{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304565 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96967f25-565a-5338-878e-00fd30055772" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Below a Curve and Above the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b1700c8-ebb4-5dbb-b5cb-e125921de9e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{sin}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304567} {:answer/id #uuid "a5606232-472f-524c-bdd6-6bbc6c44b70e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{sin}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304568} {:answer/id #uuid "31a1f447-87ee-547b-b868-fcfd68bf25d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{cos}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304569} {:answer/id #uuid "c290a8b2-23f9-5759-b431-05840a83c0eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304570} {:answer/id #uuid "082e07de-fbd0-5926-a9a8-cc87e8d22068" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\pi +\\operatorname{cos}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31a1f447-87ee-547b-b868-fcfd68bf25d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{cos}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304569} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d114066-46c2-5f55-aff3-ee0e9c8d2261" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304566}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ed8b9da1-2f9e-5b3f-b37f-5208fd9750c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-49178" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/assets/ee37408e644416b0fe2d127703e6c5b531ae469e92d4119436fbb7f2b93ef573.png)\n\nA region in the $x$-$y$ plane is bounded by the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{1}{x}$, the $x$-axis and the lines $x=1$ and $x=\\pi $, as shown above. The area of the region is" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x){|}_{1}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi )-(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡1) \\\\  & =1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{cos}⁡1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304572 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ad216da-1bcf-5b87-9436-918ef1e5015a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Above a Curve and Below the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e201c8fd-1869-5ede-b6ad-0aed0618b063" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304574} {:answer/id #uuid "c20809de-5f82-506a-904c-5a4896f05924" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304575} {:answer/id #uuid "2e68784f-1248-5cb6-84f2-9859e21acd00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304576} {:answer/id #uuid "24eb3c35-0b2a-59b8-93bf-0aa48f818997" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304577} {:answer/id #uuid "69c92cc3-1574-57cc-8792-762701e9886e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c20809de-5f82-506a-904c-5a4896f05924" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304575} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c2c475a-8897-55ec-8804-225f2b7be9a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304573}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "882a6182-51b5-5a78-824c-d594efd5fdfc" :question/math-academy-id "q-54471" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/assets/d07ef9eb8b578cd9f5f0c2c57caa44760b0a5e21d95bb0961fcff722276a7b4e.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y={x}^{2}-4$, the $x$-axis and the line $x=-2$ and $x=2$, shown above." :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}({x}^{2}-4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-4{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{-2}^{2}-4x{|}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{2}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{(-2)^{3}}{3})-4(2+2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{32}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $\\frac{32}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309583 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ad216da-1bcf-5b87-9436-918ef1e5015a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Above a Curve and Below the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ebf750f-a7d7-5d7b-be14-99ef8c708f84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309585} {:answer/id #uuid "2dd65fbf-c108-5aa2-b5db-0864d2144ceb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309586} {:answer/id #uuid "8b10a4df-93f6-5ec6-923c-886d7092f2bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309587} {:answer/id #uuid "9f6432e0-31ff-594f-aee1-d4502c1f5527" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309588} {:answer/id #uuid "1b3dd348-3beb-5331-9faa-79a9238390fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2dd65fbf-c108-5aa2-b5db-0864d2144ceb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309586} :answer-field/id #uuid "2997fc87-6dd7-53c0-8086-8d674f1010c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309584}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7fd92209-d3be-59fd-82d6-ee543e246f84" :question/math-academy-id "q-73327" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/assets/70a4f7ef7589f303924f1c48e7b0c26cd2173960847ac660199d11ae144c0afc.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$, the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$, as shown above. Find the area of the region." :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡0) \\\\  & =-(\\sqrt{2}-1) \\\\  & =1-\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $\\sqrt{2}-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309590 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96967f25-565a-5338-878e-00fd30055772" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Below a Curve and Above the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24be24bd-3344-5282-bb39-0ac712c6f651" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{64}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309592} {:answer/id #uuid "2fbe2e60-3b90-5e7d-af38-17e36de6c101" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309593} {:answer/id #uuid "b4ff8285-8cf9-50e1-99d2-6412ad098044" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309594} {:answer/id #uuid "d096a1c4-7b89-5e49-8d83-d30cdb6afa0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309595} {:answer/id #uuid "3312cc86-ed84-59ad-9fd8-8016b2208f34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{40}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309596}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2fbe2e60-3b90-5e7d-af38-17e36de6c101" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309593} :answer-field/id #uuid "127f7932-4d5f-5926-bb17-b24c318a994a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309591}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0926bed0-4f3e-528f-a5d9-117e39f32101" :question/math-academy-id "q-9978" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/assets/79889a1366311f6175a3cc736d5cd800a19a9d843daffc824d36c0690f0e3310.png)\n\nFind the area of the closed region between the curve $y=4-{x}^{2}$ and the $x$-axis, shown above." :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}(4-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4x{|}_{-2}^{2}-{\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =4(2-(-2))-(\\frac{8}{3}-(-\\frac{8}{3})) \\\\  & =16-\\frac{16}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
